    {
      "id": "77z0wbm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "13.4 Key Latin Legal Maxims"
    },
    {
      "id": "a037cpd",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Maxim</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Application in Law</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Actus reus</p>",
            "<p>Guilty act</p>",
            "<p>Criminal offence requires both actus reus (act) and mens rea (intention) to be proved</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mens rea</p>",
            "<p>Guilty mind / criminal intention</p>",
            "<p>Essential element of crime; intention to commit the act</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Audi alteram partem</p>",
            "<p>Hear the other side</p>",
            "<p>Principle of natural justice — both parties must be heard before decision</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nemo judex in causa sua</p>",
            "<p>No man shall be judge in his own cause</p>",
            "<p>Principle of natural justice — decision-maker must be unbiased</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Res ipsa loquitur</p>",
            "<p>The thing speaks for itself</p>",
            "<p>In negligence — act itself proves negligence; burden shifts to defendant</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Volenti non fit injuria</p>",
            "<p>To a willing person, no injury is done</p>",
            "<p>Defence in tort — if plaintiff voluntarily assumed risk, no liability</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Caveat emptor</p>",
            "<p>Let the buyer beware</p>",
            "<p>Buyer responsible to check goods before purchase; limited now by consumer protection laws</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Stare decisis</p>",
            "<p>To stand by things decided</p>",
            "<p>Doctrine of precedent — courts follow previous decisions of higher courts</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ex parte</p>",
            "<p>On one side only</p>",
            "<p>Proceeding or order in absence of other party</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Prima facie</p>",
            "<p>On first appearance</p>",
            "<p>Sufficient evidence to proceed; presumption until rebutted</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Locus standi</p>",
            "<p>Place of standing</p>",
            "<p>Right to bring action before court; standing to sue</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sub judice</p>",
            "<p>Under judgment</p>",
            "<p>Matter currently before court; pending adjudication</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Quid pro quo</p>",
            "<p>Something for something</p>",
            "<p>Consideration in contract — something given in exchange</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nemo dat quod non habet</p>",
            "<p>No one can give what they don't have</p>",
            "<p>Transferor cannot give better title than they possess; basis of buyer's protection</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Delegatus non potest delegare</p>",
            "<p>A delegate cannot further delegate</p>",
            "<p>Agent cannot sub-delegate unless expressly authorised; principal appoints personally</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ubi jus ibi remedium</p>",
            "<p>Where there is a right, there is a remedy</p>",
            "<p>For every legal right violated, there must be a legal remedy</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Inter vivos</p>",
            "<p>Between the living</p>",
            "<p>Transactions taking effect during lifetime of parties (vs testamentary)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
